# Privacy Policy for Sunnyside

**Effective date:** October 21, 2026

## Summary

Sunnyside works out which side of a bus, train, car, ferry or plane will be in the shade. Everything is computed on your phone. Sunnyside has no accounts, no analytics, no advertising and no servers of its own.

## What the app uses

### Your location (optional)
If you allow it, Sunnyside reads your device location once per launch to fill in your starting point. The coordinate is used only for the on-device sun calculation. It is not stored after you close the app and it is never sent to us.

If you decline, you can type a starting point instead. Nothing else changes.

### Places you type
When you search for a place, the text you type is sent to Apple Maps (MapKit) to suggest addresses and to convert a chosen place into coordinates. This happens through Apple's own services under Apple's privacy policy (https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/). Sunnyside does not add any identifier to these requests.

### Trips you save
If a future version lets you save trips, they are stored only on your device (and in your iCloud backup if you have backups enabled). We cannot read them.

## What we do not do

- We do not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers or identifiers.
- We do not track you across apps or websites.
- We do not use analytics or crash-reporting SDKs.
- We do not show ads.
- We do not sell or share any data, because we do not hold any.

## Children

Sunnyside is not directed at children under 13 and collects no personal information from anyone.

## Changes

If this policy changes, the new version will be published at the same address with a new effective date.

